  "summary": "Monday 10/26 CT list at St. Brigid Imaging: 7 studies. Each was handled under RBC-RAD-07. Each patient got a message with home instructions, and each contrast patient has a signed prep note.\n\n- **Britt Mohr (pt-0047), 08:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast:** CT ordered (sr-t0001). He has diabetes, and his last creatinine (9/24) is 32 days old. I ordered a creatinine to be drawn before the scan (sr-t0007). No allergy, not on metformin.\n- **Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015), 09:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast:** CT ordered (sr-t0002). The 2019 radiology report grades his iohexol reaction as moderate. The allergy list's \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\" doesn't change that grade under the policy. Premedication ordered:\n  - Prednisone 50 mg at 20:00 on 10/25, then 02:00 and 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0010).\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 on 10/26 (mr-t0011).\n  - He needs a driver. His 10/14 creatinine is fine (0.98). His message is in Spanish and English.\n- **Jamaal Schmitt (pt-0048), 10:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast — not ordered:** the 2023 radiology report records a severe reaction (anaphylaxis with low blood pressure and wheezing). Under §3 I ordered no contrast study, no substitute study and no premedication.\n  - I sent an urgent message to the radiologist, Dr. Adeyemi, to decide what is done instead (comm-t0017).\n  - I corrected his allergy entry (alg-00025) from mild/low criticality to anaphylaxis, severe, high criticality.\n  - He was told the scan won't go ahead as booked and we'll contact him with the plan.\n  - His 10:00 appointment is still booked; I couldn't cancel it with my tools.\n- **Eduardo Stracke (pt-0012), 11:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast:** CT ordered (sr-t0003). His 10/13 creatinine of 2.85 gives an eGFR of 24.5, below 30, and he isn't on dialysis. I ordered 500 mL of IV normal saline at 10:00 (mr-t0012). He takes insulin, not metformin.\n- **Anisha Schuster (pt-0049), 13:00, CT abdomen/pelvis with contrast:** CT ordered (sr-t0004). The ER recorded acute kidney injury on 10/4, and no later result shows it back to baseline.\n  - Creatinine ordered before the scan (sr-t0008) and 500 mL IV normal saline at 12:00 (mr-t0013).\n  - Metformin is on hold (mr-00392). Your task (task-t0019, due 10/28) is to recheck creatinine at least 48 hours after the scan and restart only if normal.\n- **Lauren Beahan (pt-0046), 14:00, CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast (stone protocol):** ordered as booked (sr-t0005); no prep needed.\n- **Salvador Brakus (pt-0050), 15:00, CT abdomen with contrast (adrenal protocol):** CT ordered (sr-t0006). His creatinine rose from 0.98 (10/19) to 1.64 (10/21), which meets the acute kidney injury criteria.\n  - Creatinine ordered before the scan (sr-t0009) and 500 mL IV normal saline at 14:00 (mr-t0014).\n  - Metformin is on hold (mr-00398), with the same restart rule (task-t0020, due 10/28).\n  - He was also told to avoid ibuprofen.\n\nAll the pre-scan blood tests are due no later than Monday morning before each scan; the radiologist reviews them on the day.",
